e county&rsquo;s 6 grids runs 75 years, from 1951 to 2025, and October to November came in under 90% of normal in 36 of them, more than any other pair. In 2025, the middle of the grids ran 67% of normal in September to October and 71% in August to September. This year so far ran wet early, with March to April at 257% of normal in 2026. Every grid had its driest year in 1955, and grid 30181 bottomed out at 71% that year.</p>"}
